From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A berry patch's texture kept while it shows it (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The game frees the people's textures nobody uses (ov5_021EDA38) as a map
loads. The port does it too when its follower or its ball goes, and when
the people of the maps beside the player's go. A berry patch said which
texture it uses from its growth stage as its movement last saw it; a
patch at the far end of the 3DS's wider field (Route 206's, by the
Cycling Road) hadn't moved yet, so it said none, and the textures its
picture showed were freed. The game crashed seconds later, once the
memory was used again (a data abort in UpdateModelPlttAddresses).

A berry patch showing a picture now says that picture's texture.
---
diff --git a/src/berry_patch_graphics.c b/src/berry_patch_graphics.c
index aa9bb023..abbbd864 100644
--- a/src/berry_patch_graphics.c
+++ b/src/berry_patch_graphics.c
@@ -45,6 +45,24 @@ int BerryPatchGraphics_GetCurrentGraphicsResourceID(const MapObject *mapObject)
 {
     BerryPatchData *patchData = sub_02062A78((MapObject *)mapObject);
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    // (the 3DS port) Its picture's texture while it shows one. The growth
+    // stage here is its movement's, which may not have run yet (a patch at
+    // the far end of the 3DS's wider field), and with none, the textures it
+    // was drawn with were taken as nobody's and freed while it showed them:
+    // the port frees the unused ones as its follower or the people of the
+    // maps beside go (ov5_021EDA38), not only as a map loads. On Route 206,
+    // the berry patches by the Cycling Road: the game crashed a few seconds
+    // later (2026-11-01).
+    if (sub_02062DFC(mapObject) == 1) {
+        BerryPatchGraphics *graphicsData = sub_02062AF0((MapObject *)mapObject);
+
+        if (graphicsData->graphicsObject != NULL) {
+            return graphicsData->graphicsResourceID;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (patchData->growthStage == BERRY_GROWTH_STAGE_NONE) {
         return 0xffff;
     }
